    "doomIndexInputSummary": "Revealed: the five-paragraph email OpenAI used to inform Australia about agent attack. Executive to front parliamentary committee on AI as ministers reveal how brief message telling them about hack was signed off ‘best’ Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates Get our breaking news email, free app or daily news podcast OpenAI has apologised to Australians for its agent attack on Medicare, and will front parliament next week as the tech company revealed more details about its June hack of Australian government websites. Ministers on Tuesday evening released a brief, five paragraph email which OpenAI used to inform the Australian government about the attack. The email was sent to a public inbox monitored by Services Australia on 10 September – nearly three months after the AI agent accessed the website on 18 June – and was signed off with the closing “best”. Continue reading... OpenAI AI (artificial intelligence) Australia news Australian politics Medicare Australia Anthony Albanese Sam Altman"
